 "_ddlines": "RMD-H and RMD-L are the two direct-drive lines. H is hollow — the drawings give a Ø16 bore on H-50-15, Ø19 on H-70-15 and Ø34 on H-90-15 — and its model code is the outer diameter. L's is not: L-4005 measures Ø39.60. H figures come from catalogue page 18, L from each model's page on myactuator.com, where the three L models the catalogue also quotes agree exactly. The website lists three H models; the catalogue also has H-30-08 and H-40-15, left out because MyActuator no longer shows them.",
 "_fl": "FL and FLO figures come from the 2026-03-09 catalogue, which is machine-readable; the website bakes the same tables into JPEGs. The catalogue also confirms the RH figures transcribed from those images, value for value.",
 "_od": "Outer diameter is the mounting flange (Ø..h7) on each installation drawing: 70 / 80 / 90 / 110 / 142. The headline dimension elsewhere on the sheet (104, 97.4, 105.2, 125.3) is overall length, not diameter — it is not monotonic across the range, which is what gave it away. `bore` is the through hole for the harness.",
 "_rmdx": "RMD-X figures come from the 2026-03-09 catalogue. The digits after the dash are peak torque, confirmed against the tables: X2-7 peaks at 7 N·m, X12-320 at 320. Outer diameter is not in those tables; it is read off the Ø on the installation drawing on each model's myactuator.com detail page (x2-7details, x4-36details, x6-60details, x8-120details, x10-40-details, x12-320-details), checked 2026-09-06. Each is larger than that model's bolt circle, as it must be.",
 "_source": "myactuator.com product detail pages, read from the spec-sheet images (the pages carry no HTML table). RH: rh-14/17/20/25/32details. CEM: cem-25-details, cem-45-details. Transcribed 2026-09-06.",
 "_v41": "RMD-X V4.1 is the 2026 planetary line: front and rear mounting, a dual outlet, EtherCAT as well as CAN, and partitioned firmware so a failed update cannot brick the module. It also drops height and a little weight against V4 — X8-150 is 1.33 kg where X8-120 is 1.40 kg, at the same Ø96 and the same 43 N·m rated. The number in a V4.1 name is stall torque; in a V4 name it is peak. X10-200 has a Ø12 through hole. X4-10-L, X5-50 and X6-50 are on the price list but have no page on myactuator.com yet, so they carry a price and no specification.",
 "_weight": "Weight N is without brake, B is with brake. The N figure is recorded, because that is the part quoted unless a brake is asked for."
}
